Ritemark Branding: theme, fonts (Phosphor + Sofia Sans), icons, about dialog, breadcrumbs; Help: Welcome opens Ritemark's welcome
Sprint 1+: Original branding patch.
Sprint 55: Rebased onto VS Code 1.117.0
  - Welcome page rewrite reapplied for upstream layout/agent surface drift
  - Brand asset includes added to gulpfile vscodeResourceIncludes (post-accessibility-signals slot)
  - rcedit branding updated to Productory at new gulpfile line position
  - codicon.css Phosphor font registration repositioned
  - workbench.startupEditor default at new contribution line position
Sprint 133 (R12): the Getting Started page retires. Its rewrite (gettingStarted.ts, gettingStarted.css,
gettingStartedGuide.css) and the startupEditor default are gone; Ritemark's welcome is a page of the extension,
and workbench.startupEditor is "none" in product.json's configurationDefaults. Every way into the page left in
gettingStarted.contribution.ts (Help: Welcome, Show All Walkthroughs, a walkthrough opening on install) runs
ritemark.welcome.open instead, and a Getting Started tab saved in an earlier session is dropped (no serializer).
Note: Binary fonts/icons (woff2, svg) handled by apply-patches.sh, not in this diff.
